# D4 task 2.5: a new model sent over MQTT without reflashing. Captured 2026-11-19 16:30 on the N16R8 DevKitC (BOARD=n16r8, main at 76c453d) with `.venv/bin/python parity/model_test.py --broker <laptop-ip> --node s3-001 --port /dev/cu.usbmodem1101 --log parity/logs/mtk/d4-2.5/model-upload-test.log`. Result 8/9: valid-upload, infer-after-upload, corrupt-refused, oversized-refused, interrupted-restarts, infer-after-bad-uploads, infer-after-reset and arena-recorded (2908 / 65536 bytes) pass. The miss, persists-after-reset, is the script reopening the port 4 s after its reset, by which time the model has already reloaded (as in D1 task 31); persists-after-reset.log shows the reload. Below: send_model.py output, then the board console.
